{"content": [{"text": "I need to count strings of length 7 over {0,...,9} with digit sum exactly 30 and no two adjacent digits equal.\n\nI'll set up a transfer-matrix / DP by position, tracking the running sum, then subtract the adjacency violations via inclusion-exclusion... actually the cleanest reliable approach is a direct DP over positions tracking (sum so far) and (last digit), but tracking last digit means 10 states. Let me instead use a generating-function with inclusion-exclusion on equal-adjacent pairs, since that reduces to counting compositions.\n\n**Approach: inclusion-exclusion on the 6 adjacency constraints.**\n\nLet the constraint \"digit i = digit i+1\" for i=1..6. Let $A_S$ = number of length-7 digit strings with sum 30 where all equalities in set $S$ hold (other positions free). By inclusion-exclusion, the count with no two adjacent equal is $\\sum_{S} (-1)^{|S|} A_S$.\n\nIf we force a set $S$ of equalities, the string breaks into \"blocks\" of forced-equal consecutive positions. If $S$ has $k$ chosen adjacencies, the 7 positions merge into $7-k$ blocks. Each block of size $b$ contributes a value that is $b \\times d$ where $d \\in \\{0,...,9\\}$ is the common digit, so a block of size $b$ contributes a multiple of $b$, namely $b\\cdot d$ with $d\\in\\{0..9\\}$.\n\nThe number of ways to choose $S$ with $k$ adjacencies that produce a specific composition of block sizes: actually each subset $S$ of the 6 gaps corresponds bijectively to a composition of 7 into ordered blocks (block sizes = run lengths determined by which gaps are \"merged\"). So summing over all $S$ is summing over all compositions of 7, with sign $(-1)^{7 - (\\text{number of blocks})}$.\n\nSo: $\\text{Answer} = \\sum_{\\text{compositions } (b_1,...,b_m) \\text{ of } 7} (-1)^{7-m} N(b_1,...,b_m)$\n\nwhere $N(b_1,...,b_m)$ = number of ways to pick $d_1,...,d_m \\in \\{0..9\\}$ with $\\sum b_j d_j = 30$.\n\nLet me define for a block of size $b$ the generating function $f_b(x) = \\sum_{d=0}^{9} x^{b d}$. Then $N$ = coefficient of $x^{30}$ in $\\prod_j f_{b_j}(x)$.\n\nLet me reorganize by the multiset of block sizes since $N$ only depends on the multiset, but the sign depends only on $m$, and the number of compositions giving a particular multiset is the multinomial. This is getting complex. Let me instead just do a **clean DP tracking last digit** — that's the most reliable. Let me verify the inclusion-exclusion against it.\n\nLet me reconsider and just compute the DP directly. I'll track, after placing each position, a table indexed by (last digit, sum). I'll carry counts. Let me compute carefully.", "type": "text"}], "index": 1, "model": "claude-opus-4-8", "role": "assistant", "type": "message"}
