rify $P_5(22)=6000$. $\\binom{26}{4}=\\frac{26\\cdot25\\cdot24\\cdot23}{24}=\\frac{358800}{24}=14950$. $\\binom{16}{4}=1820$, $5\\cdot1820=9100$. $\\binom{6}{4}=15$, $10\\cdot15=150$. $14950-9100+150=6000$ ✓. The symmetry: a length-5 digit count is symmetric about $45/2=22.5$, so $P_5(22)=P_5(23)$, and $P_5(24)=P_5(21)$ ✓. Sum $43457$ recomputed matches.\n\nI'm fairly confident. Let me also double check one of the medium terms, $3,2,1,1$ giving $N=326$, since it's a complex one. I computed $Q(R)$ values $6,16,30,41,50,48$... let me re-verify $Q(18)=50$ and $Q(21)=48$. $Q(18)$ summed $P_2$ over even args 0..18: $1+3+5+7+9+9+7+5+3+1=50$ ✓ (these are $P_2(0,2,4,...,18)$). $Q(21)$: args 21,19,17,...,3 (odd, $d_2=0..9$): $P_2$ at $17,15,13,11,9,7,5,3$ = $2,4,6,8,10,8,6,4=48$ ✓. The total $326$ stands.\n\nLet me also recheck $2,2,1^3$: $N=3943$. The largest terms w=8,9 gave 675,730. Recheck w=9: $P_2(9)=10$, $30-18=12$, $P_3(12)=73$, $10\\cdot73=730$ ✓. Sum 3943 ✓, $\\times10=39430$ ✓.\n\nAnd $3,1^4$: $N=3312$, $\\times5=16560$. $P_4(18)=670$ recheck: $\\binom{21}{3}=1330$, $4\\binom{11}{3}=4\\cdot165=660$, $1330-660=670$ ✓.\n\nThe computation is consistent. My previous answer of 222480 was incorrect; the corrected inclusion-exclusion gives 293589.\n\nLet me do one final re-add of all 15 contributions in order to be safe:\n$0, -4, -4, -4, +60, +150, +108, +96, -1004, -3912, -1460, +16560, +39430, -260742, +504315$.\n\nRunning total: $0$; $-4$; $-8$; $-12$; $+48$; $+198$; $+306$; $+402$; $-602$; $-4514$; $-5974$; $+10586$; $+50016$; $-210726$; $+293589$. ✓\n\nFINAL ANSWER: 293589", "type": "text"}], "index": 4, "model": "claude-opus-4-8", "role": "assistant", "type": "message"}
